Id: sysd005w
Severity: WARN
Category: services
Check: check_units
Fix: chmod go-w the program and its directories; keep service scripts in /usr/local/sbin.
References: systemd.service(5)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-5, CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

An enabled systemd service runs a program (an ExecStart= or another
Exec*= line) that, or a directory above which, can be written by its
group or by anyone. Whoever can write it can replace the program, and
their code then runs as the service's account (User=, root when there
is none) at its next start.

It is a WARN because its group can write it and the program is
executable.

To fix it, give the program and its directories to root (or to the
service's user), take group and other write permission off them, and
keep scripts that services run in a root-owned directory such as
/usr/local/sbin.
